content:
To,
The Public Information Officer,
{{pio_office}}

Subject: Application for information under Section 6(1) of the Right to Information Act, 2005

Sir/Madam,

I, {{applicant_name}}, residing at {{applicant_address}}, request the following information under the Right to Information Act, 2005:

{{information}}

I am a citizen of India. The application fee has been paid as follows: {{fee_details}}.

If the information requested is held by another public authority, kindly transfer this application under Section 6(3) of the Act and inform me.

Yours faithfully,

{{applicant_name}}
Date: {{date}}
Place: {{place}}

To,
{{seller_name}}

Subject: Complaint regarding {{product}} (Order/Invoice: {{order_details}})

Dear Sir/Madam,

I purchased {{product}} from you (Order/Invoice: {{order_details}}) for Rs. {{amount}}.

The problem is as follows:
{{problem}}

This amounts to a defect/deficiency in service under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. I request you to provide a {{remedy}} within 15 days of receiving this letter.

If the matter is not resolved within this time, I will be constrained to approach the National Consumer Helpline and the Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission, at your cost and risk.

Copies of the invoice and supporting documents are enclosed.

Yours faithfully,

{{customer_name}}
{{customer_contact}}
Date: {{date}}

To,
{{landlord_name}}

Subject: Request for refund of security deposit for {{property_address}}

Dear Sir/Madam,

I was your tenant at {{property_address}} and paid you a refundable security deposit of Rs. {{deposit_amount}} at the start of the tenancy.

I vacated the premises and handed over the keys on {{vacated_on}}, after clearing all rent and dues. The premises were handed over in good condition, subject to normal wear and tear.

Despite this, the security deposit has not been returned. I request you to refund Rs. {{deposit_amount}} within {{days}} days of receiving this notice, by bank transfer or cheque.

If the amount is not refunded within this period, I will be compelled to take appropriate legal action for recovery along with interest and costs.

Yours faithfully,

{{tenant_name}}
{{tenant_address}}
Date: {{date}}

To,
The Station House Officer,
{{police_station}}

Subject: Complaint and request for registration of FIR

Sir/Madam,

I, {{complainant_name}}, wish to report the following incident:

Date and time: {{incident_date}}
Place: {{incident_place}}
Accused (if known): {{accused}}

Details of the incident:
{{details}}

The above acts disclose a cognizable offence. I request you to register an FIR, investigate the matter and provide me with a free copy of the FIR.

I declare that the above information is true to the best of my knowledge.

Yours faithfully,

{{complainant_name}}
{{complainant_contact}}
Date: {{date}}

To,
The Branch Manager,
{{bank_branch}}

Subject: Report of unauthorised transaction in account ending {{account_number}}

Sir/Madam,

I, {{customer_name}}, hold an account ending {{account_number}} with your branch. I wish to report the following unauthorised transaction(s), which I did not make or authorise:

{{transaction_details}}

How it happened:
{{how_it_happened}}

I have also reported this to the cyber crime authorities (reference: {{cyber_complaint}}).

I request you to immediately block further debits, investigate the transaction and reverse the amount to my account in line with the RBI guidelines on limiting customer liability in unauthorised electronic banking transactions. Kindly acknowledge this complaint in writing.

Yours faithfully,

{{customer_name}}
Date: {{date}}
